      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Plack::Middleware::CSP versions before 0.03 for Perl send the Content Security Policy under the wrong header name, so browsers never enforce it.\n\nThe call method sets the policy in a response header named \"content-security-protocol\" instead of \"Content-Security-Policy\". Browsers ignore that header.\n\nAny cross-site scripting flaw in the wrapped application can run scripts the policy was meant to block.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
